Patch T8 oracles (rung 1b, task T8; gate G5, optional): protect eng-gpu's
counting test.

- crates/eng-gpu/tests/counters.rs joins protected.toml and
  .github/CODEOWNERS (proposal 8, amendment 31). Criterion 9
  `gpu-report-budgets` holds the per-frame counters against
  budgets.toml [gpu]; this file pins how eng-gpu counts draws, pipeline
  and bind-group switches and uploaded bytes, with passes made up for the
  test, whatever eng-render draws.
- No xtask step: criterion 9's check is the native job's `gpu-budgets`
  step (X2), and CI's test job has no GPU, where the file's tests skip.

Base: main with t10-oracles.patch and t3-oracles.patch applied (they
stack; see t10-oracles.patch). Best applied after T11, which may change
`Graph::render` to take a window's frame each frame. At the repo root, run
`git apply` with this file, then `cargo xtask quick`. Session 17's T8
entry in PROGRESS.md says how the counting test was tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

